    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193016_806262_23388" xmi:uuid="4363b575-9638-46fd-a2e4-0e2224a200cb" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454491653642_289838_42919" xmi:uuid="80de6fe3-4e2c-43a0-afee-3b445255276f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193016_806262_23388"/>
        <body>An AlternativeSolution is an object that identifies one of potentially many mutually exclusive implementations of a BreakdownElement; the BreakdownElement may be classified as functional or physical. An AlternativeSolution may refer directly to the object to be implemented or to another AlternativeSolution object. In the latter case it serves as a refinement of the referenced AlternativeSolution. &lt;note&gt; An AlternativeSolution may specify (through AlternativeSolutionRelationship with attribute &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_Breakdown.htm#AlternativeSolutionRelationship.RelationType&lt;/path&gt; RelationType&lt;/a&gt; having the values 'functionality' or 'realization') a set of objects that jointly form this implementation.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt; An AlternativeSolution may be one of its specializations FinalSolution, SupplierSolution, or TechnicalSolution. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551097070632_639101_134930" xmi:uuid="94f2e0ae-e3c4-4a8e-a2d6-f19e93bcabe3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AlternativeSolution</name>
