    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193178_171238_23729" xmi:uuid="74f693d3-87d3-443e-9db7-3ed84d63355f" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454496125019_727630_43084" xmi:uuid="64ce2c31-6d50-46d7-af83-f60e058c13ae" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193178_171238_23729"/>
        <body>A PhysicalBreakdown is a type of Breakdown that identifies a partitioning of a product into a set of BreakdownElement objects that are classified to be physical objects. A PhysicalBreakdown is a view of the constituents of a product by means of parent-child relationships. Not all constituents of the product need to be included in a PhysicalBreakdown. &lt;note&gt;Parent-child relationships are represented by BreakdownElementViewRelationship objects. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt;A PhysicalBreakdown may provide a decomposition of an automobile in terms such as body, roof, bonnet, bumpers. Such a breakdown may be different from and orthogonal to a parts decomposition.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PhysicalBreakdown</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193407_708264_24858" xmi:uuid="d2b69a7c-d08e-4f82-b72d-c07f037d6a4e" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193026_693334_23417"/>
      </generalization>
