    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193032_18036_23430" xmi:uuid="7faf882a-b3dc-43d1-abc1-465e6f6e2381" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551097420741_449634_135433" xmi:uuid="e5957a49-5e4b-4532-a462-223c4c3b7197" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454494427432_478927_43033" xmi:uuid="f7574d06-ef5e-44ed-b6d3-7c64c48683b9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193032_18036_23430"/>
        <body>A BreakdownVersionAssignment is an association between a BreakdownVersion and one or many objects of the following types: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;DocumentDefinition, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;IndividualPartView, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Occurrence, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;PartView, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;ProductClass, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;ProductConfiguration or &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RequirementView.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; </body>
      </ownedComment>
