    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193030_666945_23426" xmi:uuid="e76e2ac7-ae81-4ae5-8a86-ca8c9099ba83" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1526316715253_232368_97810" xmi:uuid="243e5736-e990-4575-82a6-c8cb7a75c4bc" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-Breakdown_element_definition-defined_version"/>
        <body>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt; &lt;p&gt;BreakdownElementVersion.Views provides the mapping of Breakdown_element_definition.defined_version&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551097186141_729346_135122" xmi:uuid="2d2b2aa7-9ac5-4320-97f8-9e6cab24900e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454493826337_596137_42990" xmi:uuid="c155f15f-66f6-48be-9c10-87272c05484b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193030_666945_23426"/>
        <body>A BreakdownElementView is a characterization of a BreakdownElementVersion in one or more application domains and for one or more life-cycle stages. A BreakdownElementView is a collector of the properties that characterize the BreakdownElementVersion in the initialContext and the additionalContexts. &lt;example&gt; The design function of a pump and its as-built function can be represented by two objects of BreakdownElementView.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>BreakdownElementView</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193427_254677_24997" xmi:uuid="09e17c66-0a08-453b-bae9-c039343f3d42" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
